<title>FRANCE: Estimated breakdown of French grain bids.</title>
<headline>Estimated breakdown of French grain bids.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Only 25,000 tonnes of soft wheat were sought through France at the lowest bid for refunds in a weekly European Union tender on Thursday, traders said.</p>
<p>Following is their estimated cumulative breakdown of soft wheat and barley bids (refunds in Ecus per tonne).</p>
<p>SOFT WHEAT</p>
<p>    Cumulative tonnage		  Refund</p>
<p>     25,000				 17.93</p>
<p>    143,000				 18.95 or less</p>
<p>    195,000				 19.25 or less</p>
<p>    486,800				 19.50 or less</p>
<p>    662,800				 21.87 or less</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Cumulative tonnage		  Refund</p>
<p>    n.a.				    30.50</p>
<p>    291,000				 31.49 or less</p>
<p>    296,000				 32.00 or less</p>
<p>No breakdown of durum bids was available.</p>
<p>French cereals office ONIC said earlier that grain exporters bid through France for 662,800 tonnes of soft wheat at refunds of 17.93 to 21.87 per tonne, 296,000 tonnes of barley at 30.50 to 32.00 Ecus and 49,800 tonnes of durum at 4.98 to 30.00 Ecus.</p>
<p>All bids are for supplies from the open EU grain market.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
